        "response": {
          "output": "Best fix: move your own settings out of the `akka.*` tree (for example under `my-app.*`). The checker only flags `akka.*` paths that have no match in Akka's `reference.conf`.\n\nIf the settings have to stay under `akka.*`, list their paths as intentional:\n\n```hocon\nakka.diagnostics.checker {\n  confirmed-typos = [\"akka.my-setting.foo\", \"akka.my-setting.bar\"]\n}\n```\n\nOnly silence settings you've decided on deliberately. Don't turn the checker off wholesale with `disabled-checks`.\n\nI took this from the `akka-diagnostics` skill notes in `claude-toolkit`, not from the Akka Diagnostics source. I also assumed your \"config checker\" is the Akka Diagnostics one. If it's a different tool, tell me which and I'll look again."
