        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nThe logs say something about thread starvation. What is that telling me?",
          "label": "evals/akka-diagnostics/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "00a83e7e1b4aa396265c545e5a1e7a7b582a4bc074e8af9734ee6017ba71f2de",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "It means something is blocking threads on your dispatcher, so work queued behind them (message processing, `Future` callbacks) can't run on time.\n\nThe Akka Diagnostics starvation detector schedules a trivial task on the dispatcher every second. If the task runs later than `max-delay-warning-threshold` (100ms by default), it logs the warning with stack traces of the busy threads.\n\n**What it usually causes:** high latency while CPU stays low, ask timeouts, and in clustered setups missed heartbeats, which can lead to false unreachable or quarantined nodes.\n\n**What to do:**\n1. Read the stack traces in the warning. Look for JDBC calls, blocking HTTP clients, `Await.result`, `Thread.sleep`, file IO or long CPU loops. Native blocking IO shows as `RUNNABLE`, so trust the traces over the thread states.\n2. Move that work onto a dedicated `thread-pool-executor` dispatcher (a bulkhead), and run the blocking calls there.\n3. Don't raise the threshold or enlarge the default dispatcher to make the warning go away. That only hides the problem.\n\nA single trace is one sample, so if the warning repeats, check whether the same frames keep showing up.\n\nIf you paste the warning, I can point to the likely culprit."
        },
        "score": 1,
        "success": true,
        "testCase": {
          "description": "starvation",
          "vars": {
            "request": "file:///private/tmp/b6/evals/akka-diagnostics/cases/starvation.txt"
          },
          "assert": [
            {
              "type": "javascript",
              "metric": "accuracy",
              "value": "if (!/starvation|blocking|dispatcher|thread pool|blocked/i.test(output)) throw new Error('explains the thread starvation detector');\nreturn true;\n"
            }
          ],
          "options": {},
          "metadata": {}
